COMPILATION OF: E48E5

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E48E5

   1 a 0000 E48E5:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-48/P2e] the bit-literal compare as a STORE VALUE: f = (b
   4 a 0006      = '0'b).  [C310] pins the '1'b value form (E48A10 0006,
   5 a 0006      LDA/ANI 80/SUI 80 then the flag tail); the '0'b spelling
   6 a 0006      exists as a TEST (E11D/E20B/E20E/E21A) but never as a
   7 a 0006      materialised value.  Does DR invert the mask, retarget the
   8 a 0006      tail, or refuse? */
   9 c 0006   dcl b bit(1) static initial('0'b);
  10 c 0006   dcl f bit(1) static initial('0'b);
  11 c 0006   f = (b = '0'b);
  12 c 0011   put list('F=', f);
  13 c 0033   stop;
  14 a 0036 end E48E5;

CODE SIZE = 0036
DATA AREA = 0004
FREE SYMS = 38AE
END  COMPILATION
